{
  "id": "06037_obieru",
  "headword": "{怯|おび}える",
  "reading": "おびえる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to be frightened, to cower",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{怯|おび}え"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be frightened, to be scared, to cower",
      "explanation": "To feel fear or terror, often showing visible signs of being afraid. Used for both sudden fright and ongoing anxiety or dread."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06037_obieru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{子供|こども}たちは{雷|かみなり}に{怯|おび}えていた。",
      "english": "The children were frightened of the thunder.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06037_obieru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{犬|いぬ}が{花火|はなび}の{音|おと}に{怯|おび}えて{隠|かく}れた。",
      "english": "The dog cowered and hid, frightened by the fireworks.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06037_obieru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{怯|おび}えた{目|め}で{彼|かれ}を{見|み}た。",
      "english": "She looked at him with frightened eyes.",
      "notes": "Uses attributive form",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). No pair verb. Pattern: Xに{怯|おび}える (be frightened of/by X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing state of fear. {怯|おび}えている = 'is scared' or 'is living in fear.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・{恐怖|きょうふ}に{怯|おび}える (cower in fear)\n・{影|かげ}に{怯|おび}える (be afraid of shadows; figuratively, be paranoid)\n・{怯|おび}えた{様子|ようす} (frightened appearance)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS: {恐|こわ}がる is more casual and common; {怯|おび}える emphasizes visible signs of fear or cowering.",
